title: "Main Types of Seventh Chords"
description: "A reference guide to the main seventh chords: maj7, 7, m7, m7♭5, and dim7, with formulas, sound, and harmonic function."
keywords: "types of seventh chords, maj7, dominant seventh chord, minor seventh chord, half-diminished seventh chord, diminished seventh chord"
categories: "Chords, Harmony"
tags: "seventh chords, chords, harmony, chord formulas"
date: 2026-06-15
intro: "A seventh chord is not one specific chord, but a whole family of chords. They share the same idea: a triad plus a seventh. But the triad, the seventh, and the fifth can differ, so Cmaj7, C7, Cm7, Cm7♭5, and Cdim7 all sound different."
reader_level: arranger
